+*   **Input:** Target reduced ranks $K_n$ for each mode, where $1 \le K_n < R_n$ [S2].
+*   **Output:** A rank-reduced approximation $\tilde{\mathcal{A}}$ represented by truncated factor matrices $\mathbf{U}^{(n)}_k \in \mathbb{R}^{I_n \times K_n}$ and a truncated core tensor $\mathcal{B}_k \in \mathbb{R}^{K_1 \times K_2 \times \dots \times K_N}$ [S2].
 
 **Data Structures:**
-*   **Factor Matrices:** Stored as 2D arrays. The $n$-th factor matrix $\mathbf{U}^{(n)}$ has dimensions $I_n \times R_n$. Columns correspond to principal components (basis vectors) ordered by importance (variance explained).
-*   **Core Tensor:** Stored as an $N$-dimensional array of size $R_1 \times R_2 \times \dots \times R_N$. Due to the all-orthogonality property, the energy is concentrated in the leading entries [S1, unofficial].
